__pycache__/
*.pyc
.pytest_cache/
tests/
.git/

# REAL BUG found and fixed 2026-09-09: these model caches are fetched
# INSIDE the Docker build itself (see the Dockerfile's fetch_*.py RUN
# steps) — but without this, whatever's already cached on the HOST from
# running tests locally gets needlessly copied into the build context
# too. Normally a few hundred MB (harmless, if wasteful); made this
# genuinely painful to ignore when the new local semantic-risk LLM cache
# (app/adapters/semantic_risk/.cache/) added ~2.4GB to every build's
# context transfer. Excluding all of them, not just the new one.
app/adapters/embeddings/.cache/
app/adapters/transcription/.cache/
app/adapters/intent/.cache/
app/adapters/semantic_risk/.cache/
